<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nuevo León</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nuevo León is a region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monterrey">Monterrey</a>. It grew from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> of León, a frontier province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> granted to Luis de Carvajal in 1579, and supplied settlers for neighbouring Nuevo Santander. After independence it became a state of Mexico, and its federalists joined the short-lived Republic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> in 1840.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuevo-leon.jpg" alt="Nuevo León" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nathaniel C. Sheetz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cerro_de_la_Silla.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
